@startuml accounts-settings-sequence
!include ../../_style/sequence.iuml
title Accounts > Settings — one change, here a new password

actor Reader
participant "SettingsPage\n+ useAuth" as Client
participant "accountRouter\n+ authenticateToken, rateLimit" as Router
participant accountController as Controller
participant accountService as Service
participant "accountRules\n+ pwdHasher" as Rules
participant passwordChanges as Changes
participant jwt as Jwt
participant userModel as UserModel
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Reader -> Client : current password, new password, again
Client -> Client : 10 characters at least, the two the same,\nthe current one written
Client -> Router : PUT /api/account/password {password, newPassword}
alt no valid session
    Router --> Client : 403, useAuth.expired(): the login page
else more than 10 changes from this address in 15 minutes
    Router --> Client : 429 {error, retryAfter}
end
Router -> Controller : changePassword(req)
Controller -> Service : changePassword(req.user.id, {password, newPassword})
Service -> Rules : isPassword(newPassword)
alt 10 characters to 72 bytes broken
    Service --> Client : 400 PASSWORD_RULE
end
Service -> UserModel : withPassword(userId)
UserModel -> DB : SELECT users (with the hash)
alt the account is gone
    Service --> Client : 404
end
Service -> Rules : verifyPassword(password, hash)
alt the current password is wrong
    Service --> Client : 401 "Your current password is not this one."
end
alt the new password is the current one
    Service --> Client : 400
end
Service -> Rules : hashWithSalt(newPassword) (bcrypt, 12)
Service -> UserModel : update(userId, {password, password_changed_at: now})
UserModel -> DB : UPDATE users
Service -> Changes : notePasswordChange(userId, at)
note right of Changes : every token issued before 'at'\nis refused from now on (403)
Service -> Jwt : generateAccessToken({id, username, email, role})
Service --> Controller : {user, token}
Controller -> Jwt : startSession(res, token)
note right of Jwt : this device keeps a session,\nthe others are signed out
Controller --> Client : 200 {id, username, email, role}
Client -> Router : GET /api/session (refresh)
Client --> Reader : a toast, the fields emptied

note over Client, DB
    PUT /account/username and PUT /account/email go the same way: the rule (isUsername, isEmail), the current
    password, nothing written when it is the same value, 409 when another account has it whatever the case
    (nameTakenByOther, emailTakenByOther, then the unique index: isTaken), UserModel.update, a new token.
    An error of the server answers 500 "Your account could not be changed right now."
end note
@enduml
